### 2. Telephone normalization logic
The only normalization lives inline in the V1 controller `addOwner` method (see below), lines 104-108:
```java
String telephone = owner.getTelephone() == null ? "" : owner.getTelephone().replaceAll("\\D", "");
if (telephone.length() != 10) {
    return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);
}
owner.setTelephone(telephone);
```
It strips all non-digits and requires exactly 10 digits, storing the normalized value. Note: `updateOwner` (line 127) does NOT normalize. There is no shared/service-level normalization helper.

### 3. Controller handling POST create (the create endpoint)
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`

