- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java` — This already encodes the target behavior. `coreRejectsDuplicateTelephone()` creates an owner, then posts a second with the same telephone and `.andExpect(status().isConflict())` (409). `functionalityAllowsDistinctTelephone()` expects distinct telephones to both succeed (2xx). The class javadoc: "telephone-unique: Reject creating an owner whose normalized telephone is already used by any other owner."
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java` — black-box base (`@SpringBootTest`, `@AutoConfigureMockMvc`, `@Transactional`, `@WithMockUser` admin). Helpers: `createOwner(body)` → `POST /api/owners`; `createOwnerOk(body)` → asserts 2xx and returns id; `ownerNode()` builds a fully-unique valid owner; `uniqueTelephone()` returns `04XXXXXXXX` (10 digits). Note the test posts a bare 10-digit telephone (already 10 digits, so the existing normalize step passes it through).
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AuditLogCapture.java` — test support (audit log capture).

### Implementation note for your change
To make `coreRejectsDuplicateTelephone` pass without breaking `functionalityAllowsDistinctTelephone`, you need a duplicate-telephone check on create returning 409. The cleanest fit given the existing structure: add a `findByTelephone`/`existsByTelephone` to `OwnerRepository` (auto-derived in `SpringDataOwnerRepository`; add stubs to the jpa/jdbc impls so they compile), check it in `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner` or in the controller's `addOwner` after normalization, and either return `HttpStatus.CONFLICT` directly from the controller or throw a new exception mapped to 409 via a new `@ExceptionHandler` in `ExceptionControllerAdvice`. The normalization must happen before the uniqueness check so that differently-formatted duplicates collide.

